<% content_for :title, "GitReward — bounties that pay themselves" %>

<section class="max-w-3xl">
  <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight">Bounties for GitHub issues that pay themselves.</h1>
  <p class="mt-4 text-lg text-slate-600">
    Maintainers fund their own issues with USDC on Base. When a PR is merged, the
    bounty disburses automatically to the contributor's linked wallet — no claim,
    no invoice, no middleman holding the money.
  </p>

  <div class="mt-6 flex gap-3">
    <%= button_to "Sign in with GitHub", github_auth_path, method: :post, data: { turbo: false },
          class: "bg-slate-900 text-white px-5 py-2.5 rounded-md font-medium hover:bg-slate-700" %>
    <%= link_to "Browse open bounties", directory_path,
          class: "px-5 py-2.5 rounded-md font-medium border border-slate-300 hover:border-slate-400" %>
  </div>

  <div class="mt-12 grid sm:grid-cols-3 gap-6 text-sm">
    <div class="bg-white p-4 rounded-lg border border-slate-200">
      <div class="font-semibold">Non-custodial</div>
      <p class="text-slate-600 mt-1">Funds sit in an open-source escrow contract, not our bank account. You only pay gas to fund.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="bg-white p-4 rounded-lg border border-slate-200">
      <div class="font-semibold">Self-refunding</div>
      <p class="text-slate-600 mt-1">No merge before expiry? The maintainer refunds themselves, permissionlessly. No one can strand your money.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="bg-white p-4 rounded-lg border border-slate-200">
      <div class="font-semibold">One neutral oracle</div>
      <p class="text-slate-600 mt-1">We turn a merge into a signed payout authorization. Honest trust model — see the <%= link_to "trust page", trust_path, class: "underline" %>.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
